cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Value-Field Theory (VFT)"
message: "If you use this theory or repository, please cite this repository."
authors:
  - family-names: "Nuno"
    given-names: "T."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >
  Value-Field Theory (VFT) is a structural framework for describing how a
  shared multidimensional real-resource world K, actor-specific accessible
  portions K_i, and actor-specific expectation-forming states P_i condition
  actions and decisions A_i. Delta K(S, tau) denotes the realized real-resource
  quantity difference over a defined target scope S and interval tau. The same
  Delta K type is used across micro and macro scales; what changes is the actor
  set, time horizon, resource scope, and accounting or aggregation rule.
  E_i[Delta K(S, tau)] denotes an actor-specific expected resource change where
  the relevant Delta K is represented on a quantitative projection for which an
  expectation is defined. Preferences, desirability, credit, beliefs, and
  related structures remain in P_i rather than being identified with the
  expectation itself. VFT does not fix a universal probability measure,
  expectation-formation equation, action-selection rule, or aggregation law.
  Economic equilibrium, budget constraints, accounting identities, surplus,
  and decentralized adjustment are treated as domain-specific projection
  candidates that require additional economic and measurement assumptions.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nuno929/vf-model"
